## Context
Filed from padme, ticket 0112 (PR #263, 2026-11-26). `scripts/raid_land.py`
calls `fg.merge(pr, head, auto=not gated and not local)`, so on an ungated
base it always passes `gh pr merge --auto`. padme has no CI and
`allow_auto_merge: false`, so the forge refused: "Auto merge is not allowed
for this repository (enablePullRequestAutoMerge)". The ticket close commit had
already been pushed and the request stayed open. The lander merged it by hand
with `--match-head-commit`, as `skills/merge/SKILL.md` step 6 allows.

The same defect was fixed for molt in 1473 (PR #2296). Author decision there
(2026-11-09): leave auto-merge off on repositories without CI and fix the
tooling, not the repository settings. raid_land, the path for both raid
Phase 7 and `/merge`, was not covered.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] on an ungated base whose repository disallows auto-merge, `raid_land.py` merges directly, pinned to the head, and reads back MERGED
- [ ] a test covers that case

## Relevant files
- `scripts/raid_land.py`, `scripts/forge.py`
